 "readings": [
  "The late-epoch pattern is tested at E24 and E32, long after the best validation loss of 384-768, which was at E4 on the seen draws d01-d10: a heavily overfit regime, unlike Jane Street's 3-epoch setting. A confirmation supports the pattern in this regime only.",
  "P1 confirmed: at E32, p* falls with width over 384-768 on the four fresh draws.",
  "P3 confirmed: the peak location moves to a smaller width from E8 to E32. A peak at a ladder end is recorded at that rung. At E8 the peak was at the top rung (768) in 4 and at the bottom rung (256) in 0 of 4 draws; at E32, at the top rung in 0 and at the bottom rung in 0. S is therefore a conservative lower bound on the shift, provided each censored curve continues beyond its ladder end in the direction it leaves it (at E8, still rising at 768; at E32, still falling with width at 256). A peak above 768 cannot be tested on the 4 GiB card.",
  "P2 not confirmed: no fall or rise over 384-768 is detected at E24 with four draws. This is not a claim of absence. Power stated in advance (four draws, 95%): 0.678 at the seen effect, 0.157 conservative, 0.247 halved.",
  "10 training articles in f01-f04 were used in September by the public-text check (Pythia-70M fine-tuning, work/runs/text-check-v02). The confirmation's models are trained from scratch with the study's own tokenizer and never see that check's model or outputs."
 ],
